        <h2>Where it comes from</h2>
        <p>Kratom grows in Thailand, Malaysia, and Indonesia. Workers there have chewed the fresh leaf or brewed it as tea for generations, for steady energy through long days, and for ease afterwards.</p>
        <p>The leaf contains naturally occurring alkaloids, the most talked-about being <b>mitragynine</b>. That’s the compound we measure, and it’s what “35 mg per gummy” refers to.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="doc__block doc__block--band">
      <h2>What people use it for</h2>
      <p>Reported experiences vary a lot between people, and by amount, food, and context. Commonly described: <b>steady energy, a lifted mood, and physical ease</b>. It is not a medicine and we make no medical claims.</p>
      <div class="warnbar">How it feels differs person to person. That variability is exactly why every Dandy gummy is portioned to an exact 35&nbsp;mg, and why our guidance is always to start with one and wait.</div>
    </section>

